<title>INDIA: Highlights of India SBI's 1996/97 performance.</title>
<headline>Highlights of India SBI's 1996/97 performance.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are details of state-owned State Bank of India's (SBI) financial results for the year ended March 31, 1997, released on Thursday.</p>
<p>	   HIGHLIGHTS OF FINANCIAL RESULTS 1996/97</p>
<p>Particulars				 1996/97     1995/96</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Profit   (Mln Rs)		     13,293.00    8,316.00</p>
<p>Return on Average Assets (%)	     0.88	  0.598</p>
<p>Return on Equity (%)			16.67	 15.22</p>
<p>Earning Per Share (Rs)		    26.66	 17.54</p>
<p>Expenses Ratio (%)			  57.54	 59.54</p>
<p>Capital Adequacy Ratio (%)		12.17	 11.60</p>
<p>Tier I Ratio (%)			     8.45	  6.90</p>
<p>Average Yield on Advances (%)	   13.43	 12.17</p>
<p>Increase in Cost of Deposits (%)	 8.19	  7.53</p>
<p>Net Interest Income (Mln Rs)	53,592.30   45,250.50</p>
<p>Interest earned less interest</p>
<p>expended in India</p>
<p>Net Interest Margin (%)		    4.01	  3.96</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom -91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
